X:14
T:Medlins Races. JHa.14
T:Blanchland Races,aka. JHa.14
T:Timour the Tartar,aka. JHa.14
T:Peter Street,aka. JHa.14
N:"Timour the Tartar" was a grand romantic melodrama in two acts
N:by the prolific Matthew Gregory Lewis (1775-1818), with music by Matthew Peter King.
N:First mounted at Covent Garden in 1811, it was a caricature of Napoleon:
N:Timour, of low origin, usurps the throne and raises up his needy relations to princely dignity.
N:The play featured horses brought onto stage.
